> f(x) = x^2 + 2x + 1
> what is f of 2?
  ucas: f(2)
9
> what is its range?
  ucas: range f
range of f:
  [0, 121]   min at x ≈ -1, max at x ≈ 10
  grid of 20001 points over [-10, 10] (default; give x a range), extrema refined at critical points
> g(x: u8) = x + 1
> what is the range of g?
  ucas: range g
range of g -> u8:
  0..255   (256 distinct values)
  fits in u8
  over all 256 points of the domain
> does g overflow?
  ucas: wrap g
wrap analysis of g:
  x + 1   (u8)
      nuw fails: unsigned wrap at 1 points, e.g. x=255
      nsw fails: signed wrap at 1 points, e.g. x=127
  end to end: differs from the mathematical result at 1 points, e.g. x=255
      exact for: 0..254
  over all 256 points of the domain
> avg(a: u8, b: u8) = (a + b) / 2
> does avg overflow?
  ucas: wrap avg
wrap analysis of avg:
  a + b   (u8)
      nuw fails: unsigned wrap at 32640 points, e.g. a=255, b=1
      nsw fails: signed wrap at 16384 points, e.g. a=127, b=1
  end to end: differs from the mathematical result at 32640 points, e.g. a=255, b=1
  over all 65536 points of the domain
> is avg commutative?
  note: commutative: avg(a, b) = avg(b, a) everywhere?
  ucas: lhs(a: u8, b: u8) = avg(a, b)
  ucas: rhs(a: u8, b: u8) = avg(b, a)
  ucas: equiv lhs rhs
lhs and rhs are equal on the domain of lhs (exhaustive)
> what is f of g of 2?
  ucas: f(g(2))
16
> let h of x be x squared
  ucas: h(x) = x^2
  ucas: show h
h(x: real) = x^2
  -> real
> what is h of 3?
  ucas: h(3)
9
> h(x) = x^3
> what is h of 3?
  ucas: h(3)
27
> what is its range?
  ucas: range h
range of h:
  [-1000, 1000]   min at x ≈ -10, max at x ≈ 10
  grid of 20001 points over [-10, 10] (default; give x a range), extrema refined at critical points
